WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.752
Tambour guides a visitor from a room they admire to a project they can describe.

2
00:00:05.011 --> 00:00:07.997
This cabinetry experience was built by Wallace Shift.

3
00:00:08.638 --> 00:00:14.615
Kitchens, baths, and built-ins lead into construction stories and a tactile material library.

4
00:00:15.263 --> 00:00:19.378
Choose a wood, add a stone, and those choices collect in a sample box.

5
00:00:20.177 --> 00:00:25.249
The investment planner explores size, construction, and scope.

6
00:00:25.509 --> 00:00:29.051
Change the choices and the illustrative planning range responds.

7
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.190
Save the range, and it travels with the samples into the consultation brief.

8
00:00:34.805 --> 00:00:41.832
Four steps gather the room, timing, style notes, and contact details for a more specific first conversation.

9
00:00:42.472 --> 00:00:43.924
The preview brings it together.

10
00:00:44.185 --> 00:00:48.447
Tambour is fictional, prices are examples, and nothing is sent.

11
00:00:48.707 --> 00:00:51.040
Inspiration and inquiry stay connected.
